<br>
Calamity is virtue's opportunity=2E
<br>
I would rather think of life as a good book=2E The further you get into =
it, the more it begins to come together and make sense=2E
<br>
Adversity has the effect of eliciting talents, which in prosperous circu=
mstances would have lain dormant=2E
<br>
Middle age is the time when a man is always thinking that in a week or t=
wo he will feel as good as ever=2E
<br>
In dreams and love there are no impossibilities=2E
<br>
To be tested is good=2E The challenged life may be the best therapist=2E=

<br>
A father is always making his baby into a little woman=2E And when she i=
s a woman he turns her back again=2E
<br>
Close by the Rights of Man, at the least set beside them, are the Rights=
 of the Spirit=2E
<br>
It sounds extraordinary but it=92s a fact that balance sheets can make f=
ascinating reading=2E
<br>
Man is the only animal that learns by being hypocritical=2E He pretends =
to be polite and then, eventually, he becomes polite=2E
<br>
What we need is not the will to believe, but the wish to find out=2E
<br>
It is human nature to think wisely and act foolishly=2E
<br>
When two men in business always agree, one of them is unnecessary=2E
